# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend configuration
#
# **There is nothing required here, and that is deliberate.**
#
# The app calls a relative `/api` and connects to `/ws/...`, and Vite
# proxies both to Django (see `vite.config.js`). The browser therefore
# believes it is talking to a single origin, which is what makes the
# httpOnly refresh cookie — scoped to `/api/auth/` with `SameSite=Lax` —
# work in development exactly as it will behind one origin in production.
#
# Pointing the client at an absolute URL instead would make the API
# cross-site, and `SameSite=Lax` cookies are not sent on cross-site
# requests. The refresh would then fail with a 401 that looks like an
# expired session rather than a config mistake. This is why no
# `VITE_API_URL` is defined: there is no supported way to set one.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` only if you need to override a value below.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dev-server port. Must match the `server.port` in `vite.config.js` and the
# `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` / `CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` in the backend `.env`.
# VITE_PORT=5173

# Where the Vite dev server proxies `/api`, `/media` and `/ws`.
# The dev proxy is configured in `vite.config.js`, which reads
# `VITE_BACKEND_PORT` (default 8000) and `VITE_BACKEND_HOST` (default
# 127.0.0.1). Change those, not a proxy target here.
# VITE_BACKEND_PORT=8000
# VITE_BACKEND_HOST=127.0.0.1

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WebSocket origin — needed ONLY when the host serving the SPA proxies
# HTTP but not the WebSocket upgrade.
#
# Leave this unset and the sockets connect to the page's own origin, which
# is correct for local development and for any single-origin deployment
# (nginx, or a host that proxies `/ws` as well as `/api`).
#
# Set it when the SPA and the API are on different hosts and the SPA's host
# cannot carry the upgrade — Vercel rewrites to an external origin are the
# case this exists for, since they proxy `/api` but not `/ws`. Without it,
# chat and notifications silently fail to connect in that deployment.
#
# This is NOT the API base URL: `/api` stays relative on purpose, because
# the httpOnly refresh cookie depends on it. Only the socket moves.
#
# Accepts http(s) or ws(s); the scheme is converted as needed.
# VITE_WS_URL=https://vibematch-api.onrender.com
